    "created_at": "2026-04-19T06:48:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-19T06:48:50Z",
    "body": "From @Hixie in a duplicate issue:\n\n> I mean, the point of `type=email multiple` is to allow for better UI than a text field. If you just want a text field, use `type=text`.\n>\n> (I don't have a strong objection to allowing it on `type=email` without `multiple`, if the spec doesn't allow it. It does seem weird if `type=url` and `type=email` without `multiple` act differently for this.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
